cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use Dynabase, please cite the article below and give the data version you used."
type: dataset
title: "Dynabase: A Database of Extreme Examples in Arithmetic Dynamics"
abstract: >-
  Dynabase is a database of extreme examples in arithmetic dynamics, related to the
  Morton-Silverman uniform boundedness conjecture, the dynamical analogue of Lang's
  conjecture on canonical heights, postcritically finite maps and maps with nontrivial
  automorphisms. It collects the known examples of extreme behavior for these problems
  and tracks the status of their subproblems by degree and field of definition.
authors:
  - family-names: Hutz
    given-names: Benjamin
    affiliation: Saint Louis University
repository-code: "https://github.com/bhutz/DynaBase"
url: "https://dynabase.org"
license:
  - GPL-3.0-or-later
  - CC-BY-4.0
keywords:
  - arithmetic dynamics
  - dynamical systems
  - preperiodic points
  - postcritically finite maps
  - canonical height
  - automorphism groups
  - SageMath
